state: will be used to filter only Wyoming (`'WY'`) and to sum births across all states.  
gender: will be used to keep only female babies (`'F'`).  
year: will be used to restrict the analysis to 2021.  
name: will be grouped‑by to study every individual given name.  
number: will be aggregated (SUM) to count babies and to compute Wyoming‑to‑US proportions.

Typical conditions:
• `state = 'WY'` (Wyoming only)  
• `gender = 'F'` (female only)  
• `year  = 2021` (year of interest)

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑final BigQuery SQL queries (all limited to 20 rows) that progressively lead to the answer.

```sql
-- 1. List a few 2021 female baby names that appear in Wyoming
SELECT name, number
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usa_names.usa_1910_current`
WHERE state = 'WY' AND gender = 'F' AND year = 2021
ORDER BY number DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. See the distinct years available for Wyoming female data
SELECT DISTINCT year
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usa_names.usa_1910_current`
WHERE state = 'WY' AND gender = 'F'
ORDER BY year DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Show every state code beginning with “W”, just to sanity‑check ‘WY’
SELECT DISTINCT state
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usa_names.usa_1910_current`
WHERE state LIKE 'W%'
ORDER BY state
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Count total female births by state for 2021 (top 20)
SELECT state, SUM(number) AS total_female_births_2021
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usa_names.usa_1910_current`
WHERE gender = 'F' AND year = 2021
GROUP BY state
ORDER BY total_female_births_2021 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Total number of female births in the whole U.S. in 2021
SELECT SUM(number) AS us_female_births_2021
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usa_names.usa_1910_current`
WHERE gender = 'F' AND year = 2021
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Top 20 female baby names nationwide in 2021
SELECT name, SUM(number) AS us_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usa_names.usa_1910_current`
WHERE gender = 'F' AND year = 2021
GROUP BY name
ORDER BY us_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Top 20 female baby names born IN Wyoming in 2021
SELECT name, SUM(number) AS wy_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usa_names.usa_1910_current`
WHERE state = 'WY' AND gender = 'F' AND year = 2021
GROUP BY name
ORDER BY wy_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Compute, for every female name, Wyoming births vs U.S. births in 2021
SELECT
  name,
  SUM(CASE WHEN state = 'WY' THEN number END) AS wy_births,
  SUM(number)                                         AS us_births
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usa_names.usa_1910_current`
WHERE gender = 'F' AND year = 2021
GROUP BY name
ORDER BY wy_births DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Add the Wyoming‑to‑U.S. proportion and sort by that proportion
SELECT
  name,
  SUM(CASE WHEN state = 'WY' THEN number END) AS wy_births,
  SUM(number)                                         AS us_births,
  SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(CASE WHEN state = 'WY' THEN number END), SUM(number)) AS wy_share
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usa_names.usa_1910_current`
WHERE gender = 'F' AND year = 2021
GROUP BY name
HAVING wy_births IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY wy_share DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL ANSWER: the female baby name with the highest Wyoming share in 2021
--    (i.e., the greatest proportion of its total U.S. births occurred in Wyoming)
SELECT
  name,
  SUM(CASE WHEN state = 'WY' THEN number END) AS wy_births,
  SUM(number)                                         AS us_births,
  SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(CASE WHEN state = 'WY' THEN number END), SUM(number)) AS wy_share
FROM `bigquery-public-data.usa_names.usa_1910_current`
WHERE gender = 'F' AND year = 2021
GROUP BY name
HAVING wy_births IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY wy_share DESC, wy_births DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

